menu "Lichen UI service"
    config LICHEN_UI_LOCK_ASSERT
        bool "Debug lock-owner check: assert when LVGL is touched without the LVGL lock (#225)"
        depends on COMPILER_OPTIMIZATION_ASSERTIONS_ENABLE
        default y
        help
            Wraps LVGL's allocator and lv_inv_area at link time: a call from a task that is neither the LVGL task nor
            inside lichen_sys_ui_lock logs the task and asserts. Armed once boot has set up the display and keyboard
            (board takes the port lock directly for that). On by default wherever assertions are enabled (a debug
            build); a build with silent or disabled assertions (a release) leaves it out, wraps and all. Cost: some
            20-30 cycles per wrapped call, well under 0.1 ms per frame.
endmenu
